w" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITA KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAIKIN INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DOMYO, NOBUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITA, KOICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DOMYO NOBUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITA KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DOMYO, NOBUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITA, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A bridge circuit (11) with four check valves (31, 32, 33, 34) is provided upstream from a receiver (10) upstream from an electric expansion valve (7). A vent pipe (12) provided with a vent valve (13) connects the receiver (10) and a pipe (24) downstream from the electric expansion valve (7). In stopping the operation, the vent valve (13) is opened and the electric expansion valve (7) is closed gradually. A predetermined time after the electric expansion valve (7) is completely closed, the compressor (4) is stopped, and the vent valve (13) is closed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon cette invention, un circuit (11) en pont à quatre clapets (31, 32, 33, 34) est ménagé en amont d'un récepteur (10) se trouvant lui-même à l'amont d'un détendeur (7) électrique. Un tuyau (12) de ventilation pourvu d'une soupape (13) d'évacuation est relié au récepteur (10) et à un tuyau (24) en aval du détendeur (7) électrique. A l'arrêt, la soupape (13) d'évacuation s'ouvre et le détendeur (7) électrique se ferme progressivement. A un moment déterminé après la fermeture complète du détendeur (7) électrique, le compresseur (4) s'arrête et la soupape (13) d'aération se ferme.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>